1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:23,560
kick a pebble and let it
fly until it gets there,

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,360
to the Kashiwa type who was joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,440
What's so good about it,
even if being full of energy makes a man,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,920
there's only winning, and one nightmare,

7
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:43,880
the unchanging streets are gentler still.

8
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,900
The crows are cawing,
so it's already getting dark, isn't it.

9
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,880
Are there really yakitori here?

10
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:10,060
Tomorrow too,
it'll end with us dropping the ball

11
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,760
It's a magazine, Bama, happiness they say,

12
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,660
I realized it by taking it easy.

13
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool,

14
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:26,400
Ryotsu VS Shiratori

15
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,400
Part-time job, grand delusion

16
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:32,720
Well then, I'm heading off first,
I'm off duty tomorrow.

17
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,420
Happy!

18
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:38,660
What the hell?!

19
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,740
We did it!

20
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:41,300
Got him!

21
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,180
Ryo-san has been captured!

22
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:43,580
Stop it!

23
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:47,020
What on earth are you doing?

24
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,260
Alone, it won't make us any money, you know!

25
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,300
I know that already.

26
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,060
If we just send it, they'll make it for us.

27
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:55,320
What?

28
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,980
Where do you think you're taking me?!

29
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:13,020
Then please write your profile here.

30
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,380
Profile?

31
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:17,440
This daily pay is pretty high, isn't it?

32
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:20,420
It's dangerous,
but these conditions are good too.

33
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:23,000
It's fine even if it's a little dangerous.

34
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,180
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

35
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,740
Hey, don't decide things on your own!

36
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,780
I said it,
but we're the victims here, you know.

37
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:32,180
Right, Yo-san has no right to speak!

38
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:36,760
If you have any special skills or qualifications,
please fill those in too.

39
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:39,460
I've got qualifications to spare, you know.

40
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:42,438
First, hazardous materials handler,

41
00:02:42,488 --> 00:02:45,160
boiler technician, and then...

42
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,540
find him a job where he can make money quickly,
would you?

43
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:53,120
Even if you say that, he has no qualifications,
no perseverance, no stamina, and no special skills.

44
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:55,700
But his pride is twice as big.

45
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,920
That's a problem, Mr. Shiratori.

46
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:59,340
Shiratori?

47
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,620
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

48
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:03,520
If you take away the pride
of this Reiji Shiratori,

49
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,580
nothing is left, you know.

50
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,340
Well, this is troublesome.

51
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,620
Anyway, a job worthy of someone like me,

52
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,220
easy and glamorous,

53
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,760
and flashy, is what you should find for me.

54
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,140
Reiji Shiratori.

55
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,140
What are you doing in a place like this?

56
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:18,000
Hey.

57
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,780
With this recession,

58
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,900
your dad's company went under again

59
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,280
So you came here

60
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,420
to look for work?

61
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,240
Sharp deduction!

62
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,700
Not that! Don't say such rude things.

63
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:34,120
This is a social study tour as part
of my education in statesmanship.

64
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:38,560
Purely to broaden my horizons as the
future president of Shiratori Tekkō.

65
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,980
Yahahaha!

66
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,820
Pick it up, you poor fool.

67
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,260
What is it?

68
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,280
Newspaper?

69
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:50,620
He's so broke now he isn't even making
counterfeit bills to pass around anymore.

70
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:52,300
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

71
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,500
Well then, that's settled.

72
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:56,980
Shiratori-san.

73
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,280
Ryotsu-san, since you know him,

74
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:03,160
could you look after Shiratori for us?

75
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:06,000
No way in hell.

76
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,940
Now that's a good idea.

77
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:11,220
Left to his own devices, Ryo-san
slacks off and skims goods on the side,

78
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:14,080
and there's no telling what he'll get up to.

79
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,340
Yeah, it's better to have
someone keeping an eye on him.

80
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,820
Working with someone like him
would be nothing but dead weight.

81
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:24,600
I can't stand working with a
crude savage like him, either.

82
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:30,000
You can't do anything on your own,
so don't be picky.

83
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,100
Hey! That's rude, isn't it, you?

84
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:37,300
To be frank,
we can't send you anywhere on your own.

85
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:41,360
I don't mind, even with you along.

86
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:44,440
Hey, Shiratori, you're backtracking
on your word way too fast.

87
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:48,260
Since you'll be in charge,
we'll add that to your allowance.

88
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:50,160
Mm...

89
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:52,840
Well then, it's settled.

90
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:54,040
Got it!

91
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,720
Decided!

92
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:57,600
Hey! I haven't agreed yet!

93
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:00,940
Please send the Yoshinoya housekeeping
group's paperwork straight to this side.

94
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:01,660
Understood.

95
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:03,040
Don't decide things without me!

96
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:03,980
Well then, shall we go!

97
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,100
Hehehe.

98
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:14,080
Here this...

99
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:17,140
Nobody will take them...

100
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,740
Speak up, speak up!

101
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,642
This newly released canned juice,

102
00:05:21,692 --> 00:05:24,120
is currently on campaign:
canned mugwort soup.

103
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,880
We're giving them out for free.

104
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:27,240
How about it?

105
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:30,760
Give it a try.

106
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,020
Newly released canned juice.

107
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,820
Canned Yomogi Juice.

108
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,460
Right now, with a novelty

109
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:41,860
Yomogi doll, Yomogi too.

110
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:43,540
It's a prize gift!

111
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,400
Idiot!

112
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,000
Look, the passersby are
scared and running away!

113
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,980
They're running because of Yomogin.

114
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,940
Because she's not cute at all!

115
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:55,240
Take it, you poor bastard!

116
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,560
Feel better now, Shiratori?

117
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,019
Good,

118
00:06:06,069 --> 00:06:09,660
now that you've calmed down,
know your place.

119
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,900
Honestly, the poor one here is you.

120
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:17,140
But this sweet mugwort drink,

121
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:19,440
what kind of name is that, anyway?

122
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:19,580
What?

123
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,600
Ugh! It's... it's disgusting!

124
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:24,280
What is this stuff!

125
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,640
Shut up!

126
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:29,760
Free samples of our new sweet mugwort drink,
here you go!

127
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:33,540
Is this allowed? Isn't handing
out something like this a crime?

128
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:37,420
Hey! You're supposed to hand these out properly,
you know!

129
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:39,600
Hey, did you drink this?

130
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:41,340
Of course I did!

131
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:42,980
It's really awful, isn't it?

132
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:45,460
"Yeah"? That's not the right answer!

133
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,740
Just hand them out to the world already,
will you?

134
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,980
Whether they taste good or bad,
it's none of your business, right?

135
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:54,720
Well said.

136
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,760
We're handing them out to everyone,
no exceptions, Shiratori!

137
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,100
Because this tastes like a puddle, you know!

138
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:02,460
It's not canned juice,
it's canned puddle water.

139
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,340
I guess that must be
the president over there.

140
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,160
Going great!

141
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:11,900
I don't want to be an accomplice in
spreading something this awful to the world.

142
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,940
You're still going on about that?

143
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,760
You're going to hit the mugwort doll's mugwort head,
aren't you!

144
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:19,860
What's the matter?

145
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,820
Is there some problem with
our sweet mugwort juice?

146
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,660
No, there's no problem at all, President.

147
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:29,200
Well, no, I'll say it: bad is bad.

148
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:32,500
I've never drunk anything
this awful in my life.

149
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,880
What? The mugwort juice is bad?

150
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:37,260
Yes, it's mabui!
This mugwort juice is mabui!

151
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,640
I mean it's cool, President!

152
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,280
Yes, yes, yes, that's what you'd
expect from an advertising agency.

153
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,440
They really know what young people think.

154
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,500
Now he's definitely said our
sweet mugwort juice is bad.

155
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:50,320
Shiratori, you wretch!

156
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,720
What are you doing to the mugwort?

157
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:55,780
If you like it so much,
pour it over yourself.

158
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:57,820
President.

159
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,860
I'm very sorry.

160
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,620
You two are both fired!

161
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:06,280
We've gone and taken on a real burden!

162
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:09,920
At this rate,
how long will it take to earn back the debt?

163
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,960
Stack the cargo unloaded from the container

164
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,100
starting from the back
of the warehouse, please.

165
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,640
Any questions?

166
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,020
Understood, all clear.

167
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:23,060
Hey, aren't those Armani Valentino?

168
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:24,920
Shiratori.

169
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:28,400
Shiratori Reiji is the kind of
man who should be watched by people.

170
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,180
Locking someone like him up
in a musty warehouse like this

171
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:33,380
is such a waste of treasure.

172
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,860
Hey, anything's fine.

173
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:38,640
I'll take care of it perfectly.

174
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:39,200
Really?

175
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:40,540
Then I'm counting on you.

176
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,300
Mm...

177
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:45,320
What are you doing?

178
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:49,900
Listen, Shiratori, if you screw up again,
I'm done covering for you.

179
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:54,160
You're the one who only gets work because you're stuck with me,
aren't you?

180
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,840
I'd like a little gratitude, you know.

181
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:01,880
Gratitude? Listen, if you asked
anyone who just saw this situation,

182
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:06,200
all hundred of them would say that
you're the one causing trouble.

183
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:10,420
Even if I give you a hundred steps of
leeway and say I'm the one causing trouble,

184
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:12,920
someone as magnificent as me

185
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:15,200
may be a super-pauper now, but

186
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,420
this super-cool Reiji Shiratori

187
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:22,680
causing a little trouble for a super-poor,
sweaty slob like you,

188
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:25,300
nobody calls that trouble, you know.

189
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,780
Because

190
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:29,680
Because I'm Reiji Shiratori, after all!

191
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,260
I can't take this anymore.

192
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:34,760
Why don't you go sunbathe or something?

193
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:38,380
Unfortunately, the weather's bad,
so it's not sunbathing weather, is it?

194
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:45,040
Dangerous, dangerous, dangerous!

195
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,620
Come on, come on!

196
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:47,740
Okay, stop!

197
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:56,140
Hey, look, there's a gap at the back.

198
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,860
If you don't stack them properly,
it's all going to come down.

199
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:02,820
As long as this stuff stays under a roof and isn't hit by wind and rain,
that's all that matters.

200
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:06,400
Just stack the front row
neatly and nobody will notice.

201
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:11,860
I'm too delicate and sensitive
for this kind of thing.

202
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:15,120
It gives me chills down my
back and makes my skin crawl.

203
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:17,780
Force it up or whatever,
just stand them up however you like.

204
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:21,320
Why do I have to be
Shiratori's counterweight?

205
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:26,440
By rights, I should be the one slacking off
and someone else should be doing the work.

206
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:29,640
Hey, the box is facing
the wrong way over there.

207
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:33,020
This one's box is tilted
and about to fall over.

208
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,820
This box and that box are different kinds.

209
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:44,240
How about that? My sense of balance,
honed by years of gaming.

210
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:48,260
There's a big hole in the middle, see?

211
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,900
Look, this side and that side
are both about to collapse.

212
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,660
For this kind of thing, you do it like this.

213
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,640
There, now it won't collapse.

214
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,280
It's collapsing!

215
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,940
You two!

216
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:21,020
You're fired!

217
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:32,720
If it were just me,
I'd have paid off the national debt by now

218
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:36,200
and be taking a bath, eating,
and playing games by now.

219
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,840
Thanks to this guy,

220
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:41,760
I can't stand unstable places like this.

221
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:45,380
I've always hated seesaws and swings too.

222
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:49,680
Shut up, get up and push up quickly!

223
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:56,780
Whoa, it's shaking, it's shaking!

224
00:11:56,780 --> 00:12:00,900
Hey, hey, careful, that's dangerous, Rongen!

225
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:05,080
Jobs like this should be left to
the people who love high places.

226
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:08,560
Surely there's a job better
suited to people like us!

227
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:12,760
Stop it! That's creepy!
Anyway, you're in no position to be picky!

228
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,534
Then let me ask you this,

229
00:12:14,584 --> 00:12:17,440
what kind of job do you think suits you?

230
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,878
Well... something richer,

231
00:12:19,928 --> 00:12:22,320
more high-society,
celebrity, and glamorous...

232
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,700
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

233
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:25,540
Filthy! What are you doing!

234
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:27,838
Listen! Even if you're rich right now,

235
00:12:27,888 --> 00:12:30,620
you're not high-society, you're not a celebrity,
and you're certainly not Malibu!

236
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,660
Until the window cleaning is finished,
not even a corpse gets down!

237
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,660
Stop daydreaming and wipe quickly,
you octopus!

238
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:36,500
Octopus?

239
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,880
Don't do it like that,
that's not what I mean.

240
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,640
Wipe in straight lines, dammit.

241
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,080
That's just doing the work twice, you idiot.

242
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,500
But you can't just say that.

243
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:52,220
I've never done anything
like this before, so.

244
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,240
Come on.

245
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,860
Alright, alright already.

246
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,140
Enough already, just sit down over there.

247
00:12:58,140 --> 00:12:59,800
Use this to run the gondola.

248
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,600
Is it this one I press?

249
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:04,300
Th-this one!

250
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,480
No, it's scary up here!

251
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,820
Alright!

252
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:11,920
Haven't you already blown the top?

253
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,380
Press the bottom one, the bottom!

254
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:16,420
It's high, it's scary,
it's high, it's scary!

255
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,880
It's high, it's high, it's scary!

256
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,880
Then go slower, you idiot!

257
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,020
Eek, it's scary!

258
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,300
You idiot, Shiratori!

259
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,980
At this rate, it's going to blow, damn it!

260
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:27,840
Done!

261
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,840
That's odd.

262
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,200
Did it break, I wonder?

263
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:38,960
Move, damn it!

264
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:18,300
Hey, this is the rich, high-class,
celebrity, glamorous job,

265
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:19,820
don't complain.

266
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:24,040
This is the job I got you
based on what you wanted.

267
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:26,400
If you don't like it,
want to ride the gondola again?

268
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:30,620
Or go up high on the gondola?

269
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,420
You could even go to space, too.

270
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:34,900
That's...

271
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:36,300
That's, no.

272
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:38,800
Then stop your whining and get to work!

273
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:40,750
The F40,

274
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,680
I was this one's owner
just until recently, too.

275
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,371
Hey,

276
00:14:45,421 --> 00:14:49,600
It's converted to automatic,
just like your car.

277
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,460
I miss those days.

278
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:58,040
Back then, the world was mine.

279
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:04,360
Unfortunately, back then and now,
the world belongs to everyone.

280
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:22,220
A customer just like you has arrived!

281
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:26,440
Here, pick it up, pick it up...
ding-dong, Nissho-kun!

282
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:29,620
Well, well, we've been expecting you.

283
00:15:29,620 --> 00:15:34,920
Mr. Michio Patrick Kujaku,
president of the Kujaku Estate Group.

284
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,120
It's bound to be counterfeit money anyway.

285
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:43,220
Stop it! Do you have no pride at all?

286
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:44,720
What are you talking about!

287
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:48,840
You were doing the exact same thing until just the other day,
weren't you!

288
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:53,220
Listen, we're here to make money!

289
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,971
Your pride,
which won't earn us a single penny,

290
00:15:56,021 --> 00:15:58,000
go feed it to the crows!

291
00:15:58,400 --> 00:15:58,960
Money, money!

292
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:05,120
What about my F40?

293
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,840
Yes, sir! It's already on standby!

294
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:10,640
Put it on Daddy's tab, okay?

295
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,300
Certainly.

296
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:15,320
Your car will be brought right over,

297
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,680
Ryotsu-kun.

298
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:17,500
Yes, yes.

299
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:19,980
There you are.

300
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,960
Bring Mr. Kujaku's F40 over here.

301
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,000
Certainly.

302
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:26,220
I was in charge of the F40's
maintenance and inspection.

303
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,660
My name is Ryotsu.

304
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:29,560
I look forward to working with you.

305
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,140
Ryotsu-kun, is it?

306
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,000
Hang onto this.

307
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,720
Grunyun.

308
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:37,480
Hurry up and bring the car around.

309
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,280
Yes, right away!

310
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,160
Okey-dokey.

311
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:42,980
Shiratori!

312
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:45,340
My F40...

313
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:48,720
Hey, where do you think you're going?

314
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:50,660
Hurry and bring him back.

315
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:51,040
Yes.

316
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,220
Shiratori.

317
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:55,940
Wait a minute.

318
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:59,560
If you so much as scratch the car,
that's the end of it.

319
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,640
Get out of the car, now.

320
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,340
No.

321
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:02,260
"No," you say?

322
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,460
You don't have the authority to do that!

323
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:06,120
I'm never handing it over.

324
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,160
Besides, it's not even your car!

325
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:15,380
You're just angry at yourself, aren't you?

326
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:19,140
That has nothing to do
with him or this F-40.

327
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:21,220
Stop taking it out on people.

328
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,260
No way, I said no!

329
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,240
My F-40!

330
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:56,360
!

331
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:05,200
Stop following me, you plague god!

332
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,340
That's a terrible thing to say.

333
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,400
Terrible?

334
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:12,700
You're a poor man, and you always have been,

335
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,880
while I was rich to begin with.

336
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,500
You're insensitive, and I'm sensitive,

337
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:22,900
so naturally we have different
resistance to the hardships of the world.

338
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:25,160
In a situation like that,
my sense of justice

339
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:26,840
Sense of justice?

340
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:27,600
Yeah.

341
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:31,860
Don't try to glorify the nonsense
you pulled after all this time!

342
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:34,080
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow

343
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,960
Fine! Stop clinging to
me any more than this!

344
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:38,360
Fine, got it!

345
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:45,160
But you need me!

346
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,060
What?

347
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:49,230
You can't do it alone...

348
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,380
You can't do it alone...

349
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,760
I can live on my own without your help!

350
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:36,940
Hey, you there!

351
00:19:38,860 --> 00:19:40,160
Don't zone out!

352
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:48,820
I can't even do a simple
job like this properly.

353
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:53,100
Stop moping over every little
thing and just watch carefully.

354
00:19:57,200 --> 00:20:01,280
Just like you said,
I was taking my frustration out on him.

355
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,960
Him?

356
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:07,120
It was like looking at my own past self.

357
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,700
I couldn't stand it, and I also envied him.

358
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:16,240
Until now, I was a foolish,
immature ugly duckling.

359
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:17,678
Shiratori,

360
00:20:17,728 --> 00:20:23,360
Look at you, now that you're broke, you
can actually say something halfway sensible.

361
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,020
I'm perfectly normal.

362
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:31,220
Or rather, my true self is a quiet,
modest person.

363
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,680
Until now, as the heir to Shiratori Tekkō,

364
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:39,020
I was just putting on a brave front,
trying my hardest not to show weakness.

365
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,400
Now I've finally realized that.

366
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:45,360
That discovery means nothing to humanity,

367
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,440
but it's a big step for me. Yeah.

368
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:50,160
Mm.

369
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,980
It came off.

370
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:03,700
Maybe I'll try to master this job. Not that
it's really a job you can master or not...

371
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:08,860
I don't think so, anyway. I'm sorry for
all the trouble I've caused you until now.

372
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:10,880
Yeah. But I've changed.

373
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,880
The old Shiratori Reiji is dead.

374
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,340
So keep watching the new me.

375
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,600
Shiratori!

376
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,040
Ryo-san...

377
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,800
Not bad, you know.

378
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:43,200
So did you manage to pay off your debts?

379
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:45,760
Not yet.

380
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:50,400
On the contrary, my many failures
have grown the debt about tenfold.

381
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:55,200
From now on, I plan to work
hard and pay it back bit by bit.

382
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:58,700
Is that an amount you can
pay back by working bit by bit?

383
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,780
You're awfully calm, Ryo-san.

384
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:04,460
Because I received something
precious that money can't buy.

385
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:08,980
Something money can't buy? Senpai,
you actually had something like that?

386
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,602
Nakagawa,

387
00:22:11,652 --> 00:22:15,260
A friendship between men is
a treasure beyond all others.

388
00:22:15,260 --> 00:22:17,560
A friendship between men?

389
00:22:18,180 --> 00:22:18,950
Wait, senpai,

390
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:22,280
you worked with Reiji Shiratori, didn't you?

391
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:26,680
So does that mean a friendship
between men blossomed with Shiratori?

392
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:29,940
He's changed.

393
00:22:29,940 --> 00:22:31,161
Listen, Reiko,

394
00:22:31,211 --> 00:22:34,300
don't judge a man by first impressions.

395
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:41,120
You know, some guys hide a pure,
steady soul beneath a flippant face.

396
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:44,220
That's the kind of man he is.
That kind of man.

397
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:50,240
No way.

398
00:22:56,820 --> 00:22:59,220
Shiratori, what on earth happened?

399
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:02,500
My dad's company has been revived.

400
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:06,720
So we're back to living the rich,
celebrity life again.

401
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:07,700
What?

402
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:12,300
Public funds injected
into Shiratori Iron Works.

403
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:13,140
I see.

404
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:15,560
Well, that's just unfair.

405
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:18,960
Here you go, Reiko-san, accept my love!

406
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:24,580
How about a Caribbean cruise on
Daddy's yacht on my next day off?

407
00:23:26,140 --> 00:23:28,180
You haven't changed at all.

408
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:32,880
Sure enough,
this is what Reiji Shiratori is really like.

409
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:35,220
Nya-ha-ha-ha-ha!

410
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:37,480
Hiroeru Binbōrīn!

411
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:41,220
Nya-ha-ha-ha-ha!

412
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:44,000
U-hu-hu-hu-hu.

413
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,700
Oh well, never mind.

414
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:47,340
Uhihihihi.

415
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:55,360
It's as if someone is calling,

416
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,960
an afternoon after the rain.

417
00:23:59,220 --> 00:24:04,540
I walked looking back,
led by the hand of Gacha.

418
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:11,560
That strange feeling I had back then.

419
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:16,960
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

420
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:22,720
I tried walking only on the black ones.

421
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:30,880
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

422
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:38,360
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

423
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:49,100
Turn that corner, you'll see,
you'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

424
00:24:50,860 --> 00:24:53,760
Over there is Kameari.

425
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,080
Surely it's Kameari.

426
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:02,420
Everyone, come on over to our town!

427
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:06,980
Over there, there's Kame-ari,

428
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:10,220
surely there's Kame-ari.

429
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:15,480
Everybody come on over to our town!

430
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:17,080
Thank you!

431
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,840
Me, appearing in a commercial?
Okay! Leave it to me!

432
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:28,400
I knew it, people really do notice!

433
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:31,520
Chief, won't you please look at
my good points a little more too!

434
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:33,380
That's impossible! No way!

435
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:37,140
Next time: Honest Men, Both of Us!
See you then!

436
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:40,700
Over there, there's a wall!

437
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:43,980
Well, surely there's a wall!

438
00:25:45,540 --> 00:25:49,380
Everybody come on over, to our town!

439
00:25:50,380 --> 00:25:50,820
Thank you!

440
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:54,000
Thank you for watching.

